module

public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Rank
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.Rodicio.LocalReduction
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-! # The rank step of Stacks Tag 0FCW

Stacks Tag 0FCW characterizes a flat, essentially-of-finite-type local algebra with perfect
diagonal as the localization of a smooth algebra. Its proof runs through Rodicio's theorem
(Stacks Tag 09PV): writing `B = R/K` with `R` a localization of `A[x₁,…,x_n]` and
`𝔪 ⊂ R ⊗_A R` for the maximal ideal lying over that of `B`, one obtains ideals
`I ⊆ J ⊆ (R ⊗_A R)_𝔪` to which Tag 09PV applies, so that `I/𝔪I → J/𝔪J` is injective. The
source then converts that injectivity into a statement about the Jacobian matrix:

> The injectivity of `I/𝔪I → J/𝔪J` and the remarks made above forces the matrix `(aᵢⱼ)` to
> have maximal rank `r`.

This file proves exactly that conversion, as a statement about a local ring and two of its
ideals and nothing else. In the source's notation, `u` is the family `f₁ ⊗ 1, …, f_r ⊗ 1` and
`v` the family `1 ⊗ f₁, …, 1 ⊗ f_r` — jointly a minimal system of generators of `I`, so their
`2r` classes are linearly independent in `I/𝔪I` — while `w` is the family
`x₁ ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ x₁, …, x_n ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ x_n` inside `J`, and `g` is the matrix of the identities
`fᵢ ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ fᵢ = ∑ⱼ gᵢⱼ (xⱼ ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ xⱼ)` whose residues are the partial derivatives
`∂fᵢ/∂xⱼ`.

No hypothesis on how `J` is generated is needed: `w` is only required to consist of elements of
`J`, which is weaker than the source's "`J` is generated by the `fᵢ ⊗ 1` together with the
`xⱼ ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ xⱼ`".

## Main results

* `StacksDraft.Rodicio.mem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_injective_mapQ` — the elementwise reading of
  Rodicio's conclusion: an element of `I` landing in `𝔪J` already lies in `𝔪I`. This is the
  converse of `StacksDraft.Rodicio.injective_mapQ_of_mem_maximalIdeal_smul_top`.
* `StacksDraft.Rodicio.mem_maximalIdeal_of_sum_mul_mem_maximalIdeal` — the rank step in
  elementwise form: a relation among the rows of `g` modulo `𝔪` has all its coefficients in `𝔪`.
* `StacksDraft.Rodicio.linearIndependent_residue_of_injective_mapQ` — the rows of `g` are
  linearly independent over the residue field.
* `StacksDraft.Rodicio.rank_residue_eq_of_injective_mapQ` — equivalently, the residue matrix has
  maximal rank `r`.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis of minimality is stated as linear independence over `S ⧸ 𝔪` of the `2r` classes
in `I ⧸ 𝔪 • ⊤`, which is Mathlib's spelling of "a minimal system of generators of `I`" once
Nakayama has been applied. It is stated over `S ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S` rather than over
`IsLocalRing.ResidueField S`: the module structure of `I ⧸ 𝔪 • ⊤` over the plain quotient ring
is found by instance search, while `ResidueField` is a separate definition carrying its own field
structure and no such instance exists for it. Linear independence needs only a ring, so nothing
is lost. The conclusions, by contrast, are stated over `ResidueField S`, because `Matrix.rank`
asks for a field.

The three conclusions are each proved from the elementwise statement rather than from one
another, so that no transport between the two spellings of the residue field is needed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FCW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FCW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

namespace StacksDraft.Rodicio

universe u

variable {S : Type u} [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing S]

/-- **The elementwise reading of Rodicio's conclusion.** If the canonical map `I/𝔪I → J/𝔪J` is
injective, then an element of `I` whose image lies in `𝔪J` already lies in `𝔪I`.

This is the converse of `StacksDraft.Rodicio.injective_mapQ_of_mem_maximalIdeal_smul_top`, and it
is the form in which Rodicio's theorem is used. -/
public theorem mem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_injective_mapQ
    (I J : Ideal S) (hIJ : I ≤ J)
    (hinj : Function.Injective
      ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)).mapQ
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S J))
        (Submodule.inclusion hIJ)
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ (Submodule.inclusion hIJ))))
    (x : I) (hx : (x : S) ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • J) :
    x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I) := by
  have h0 : Submodule.inclusion hIJ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S J) := by
    rw [Submodule.mem_smul_top_iff]
    exact hx
  have h1 : ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)).mapQ
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S J))
      (Submodule.inclusion hIJ)
      (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ (Submodule.inclusion hIJ)))
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = 0 := by
    rw [Submodule.mapQ_apply]
    exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).2 h0
  have h2 : (Submodule.Quotient.mk x :
      I ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I))) = 0 :=
    hinj (by rw [h1, map_zero])
  exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).1 h2

/-- **The rank step of Stacks Tag 0FCW, in elementwise form.** Let `u` and `v` be families of `r`
elements of `I` whose `2r` classes are linearly independent in `I/𝔪I`, let `w` be a family of `n`
elements of `J`, and suppose `uᵢ - vᵢ = ∑ⱼ gᵢⱼ wⱼ`. If `I/𝔪I → J/𝔪J` is injective, then any
family `c` of coefficients with `∑ᵢ cᵢ gᵢⱼ ∈ 𝔪` for every `j` already has every `cᵢ` in `𝔪`.

The element `z = ∑ᵢ cᵢ (uᵢ - vᵢ)` lies in `I`, and rewriting it as `∑ⱼ (∑ᵢ cᵢ gᵢⱼ) wⱼ` exhibits
it in `𝔪J`; injectivity puts it in `𝔪I`, and linear independence of the classes of `u` and `v`
then forces the coefficients `cᵢ` and `-cᵢ` to vanish modulo `𝔪`. -/
public theorem mem_maximalIdeal_of_sum_mul_mem_maximalIdeal
    (I J : Ideal S) (hIJ : I ≤ J)
    (hinj : Function.Injective
      ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)).mapQ
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S J))
        (Submodule.inclusion hIJ)
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ (Submodule.inclusion hIJ))))
    {r n : ℕ} (u v : Fin r → I) (w : Fin n → J)
    (hmin : LinearIndependent (S ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S)
      (fun k : Fin r ⊕ Fin r => (Submodule.Quotient.mk (Sum.elim u v k) :
        I ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)))))
    (g : Fin r → Fin n → S)
    (hg : ∀ i, (u i : S) - (v i : S) = ∑ j, g i j * (w j : S))
    (c : Fin r → S)
    (hc : ∀ j, ∑ i, c i * g i j ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S) :
    ∀ i, c i ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S := by
  set P : Submodule S I := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I) with hP
  set z : I := ∑ i, c i • (u i - v i) with hz
  have hzval : (z : S) = ∑ j, (∑ i, c i * g i j) * (w j : S) := by
    have h1 : (z : S) = ∑ i, c i * ((u i : S) - (v i : S)) := by
      rw [hz]; push_cast; exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by ring
    rw [h1]
    simp only [hg, Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_mul, ← mul_assoc]
    exact Finset.sum_comm
  have hzmem : z ∈ P := by
    refine mem_maximalIdeal_smul_top_of_injective_mapQ I J hIJ hinj z ?_
    rw [Ideal.smul_eq_mul, hzval]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ => Ideal.mul_mem_mul (hc j) (w j).2
  have hq : Submodule.mkQ P z = 0 := (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).2 hzmem
  have hscalar : ∀ (a : S) (x : I ⧸ P),
      a • x = (Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S) a) • x := fun a x => by
    rw [← Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul]
  set d : Fin r ⊕ Fin r → S ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S :=
    Sum.elim (fun i => Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S) (c i))
      (fun i => -(Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S) (c i))) with hd
  have key : ∑ k : Fin r ⊕ Fin r, d k •
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk (Sum.elim u v k) : I ⧸ P) = 0 := by
    rw [Fintype.sum_sum_type]
    simp only [hd, Sum.elim_inl, Sum.elim_inr]
    rw [← hq, hz, map_sum]
    simp only [map_smul, map_sub]
    rw [← Finset.sum_add_distrib]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    rw [smul_sub, neg_smul, ← sub_eq_add_neg, ← hscalar, ← hscalar]
    rfl
  have hzero := Fintype.linearIndependent_iff.mp hmin d key
  intro i
  have h := hzero (Sum.inl i)
  simp only [hd, Sum.elim_inl] at h
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.1 h

/-- **The rank step of Stacks Tag 0FCW.** In the configuration above, the `r` rows of the matrix
`g` are linearly independent over the residue field of `S`. -/
public theorem linearIndependent_residue_of_injective_mapQ
    (I J : Ideal S) (hIJ : I ≤ J)
    (hinj : Function.Injective
      ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)).mapQ
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S J))
        (Submodule.inclusion hIJ)
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ (Submodule.inclusion hIJ))))
    {r n : ℕ} (u v : Fin r → I) (w : Fin n → J)
    (hmin : LinearIndependent (S ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S)
      (fun k : Fin r ⊕ Fin r => (Submodule.Quotient.mk (Sum.elim u v k) :
        I ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)))))
    (g : Fin r → Fin n → S)
    (hg : ∀ i, (u i : S) - (v i : S) = ∑ j, g i j * (w j : S)) :
    LinearIndependent (IsLocalRing.ResidueField S)
      (fun i : Fin r => fun j : Fin n => IsLocalRing.residue S (g i j)) := by
  rw [Fintype.linearIndependent_iff]
  intro a ha
  choose c hc using fun i : Fin r => IsLocalRing.residue_surjective (a i)
  have hrow : ∀ j, ∑ i, c i * g i j ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S := by
    intro j
    rw [← IsLocalRing.residue_eq_zero_iff]
    have := congrFun ha j
    simpa [hc] using this
  have hmem := mem_maximalIdeal_of_sum_mul_mem_maximalIdeal I J hIJ hinj u v w hmin g hg c hrow
  intro i
  rw [← hc i, IsLocalRing.residue_eq_zero_iff]
  exact hmem i

/-- **The rank step of Stacks Tag 0FCW, as a rank.** In the configuration above, the matrix of
residues of `g` has maximal rank `r`. -/
public theorem rank_residue_eq_of_injective_mapQ
    (I J : Ideal S) (hIJ : I ≤ J)
    (hinj : Function.Injective
      ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)).mapQ
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S J))
        (Submodule.inclusion hIJ)
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ (Submodule.inclusion hIJ))))
    {r n : ℕ} (u v : Fin r → I) (w : Fin n → J)
    (hmin : LinearIndependent (S ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S)
      (fun k : Fin r ⊕ Fin r => (Submodule.Quotient.mk (Sum.elim u v k) :
        I ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S • (⊤ : Submodule S I)))))
    (g : Fin r → Fin n → S)
    (hg : ∀ i, (u i : S) - (v i : S) = ∑ j, g i j * (w j : S)) :
    (Matrix.of fun (i : Fin r) (j : Fin n) => IsLocalRing.residue S (g i j)).rank = r := by
  have h := (linearIndependent_residue_of_injective_mapQ I J hIJ hinj u v w hmin g hg).rank_matrix
  rw [Fintype.card_fin] at h
  exact h

end StacksDraft.Rodicio

end
